Trap resolution:
```js
async function tryAttackTraps(defSide, attacker, target) {
  const trapInst = firstApplicableTrap(defSide, attacker, target);
  if (!trapInst) return {negated:false};
  const id=trapInst.id;
  removeTrapToGY(trapInst);
  addLog('trap', `${name}発動！`);
  render(); await sleep(450);
  if (id==='ambush') { destroy(attacker); return {negated:true}; }
  if (id==='mirror') { damage(attacker.owner,800,'鏡の盾'); return {negated:true}; }
  if (id==='morale' && target) { target.boost+=1000; ... return {negated:false}; }
  return {negated:false};
}
```
Need trap remains? Consumed. For morale, boost only for this battle; after battle subtract 1000. Implement local temp boost: set target.tempBoost +=1000 used in effDef/effAtk, subtract after. Simpler add to boost and after battle subtract; but boost clears at end anyway. It might affect subsequent attacks that turn; minor. Do `target.boost += 1000` and after battle `target.boost -= 1000` if still exists. Fine.

